      "analysis_required": "Stable native later boards establish a complete ten-piece ending after e8=R: White Ka1/Re8/Nb3/a2/a3/c4/f5 versus Kc3/Be5/c2. Bf6/Re6/Bg7/f6 replays the illustrated continuation with every pawn preserved. It is the same composition in JGpoYRNZtb8 and Q5D3UZNTWbc; the music-only clip supplies no chess narration. Earlier e8=N, b8=B and the final e8=R are separate promotions in the same longer study, not one pawn changing piece type. This later rook conversion still needs complete outcome proof. A bounded checks/captures search did not certify f6. A separate twelve-ply search using local Stockfish only to suggest two candidate moves at each White choice also did not produce a complete exact certificate (248 visited nodes and 32 supported leaf probes). Neither search failure is a draw judgment, and the engine estimate is not proof. Exact root/intermediate outcomes, omitted bishop/king replies, the c1 promotion defenses and the earlier stalemate comparisons remain pending. Do not drop a2/a3/c4/f5 or Black c2 to fit tablebase coverage."
